        "description": "Histopathologic confirmation of abnormal airway tissue proliferation with cystic structures",
        "category": "major",
        "requiredForDiagnosis": true
      },
      {
        "id": "clinical-respiratory-symptoms",
        "description": "Respiratory distress or recurrent pulmonary infections in neonate or infant",
        "category": "supportive",
        "requiredForDiagnosis": false
      }
    ],
    "minimumForDiagnosis": "Presence of characteristic cystic or solid lung mass on imaging plus histopathologic confirmation",
    "notes": "Prenatal ultrasound and CT imaging are critical for early diagnosis; histopathology is gold standard."
